original loading of metal alloy in silica gel; titrated reducing capacity
4.9 mmol electrons= 2.45 equiv40) were placed under an inert atmosphere
(in a He drybox). To this flask was added 10 mL of anhydrous THF, and the
mixture was stirred at room temperature for 6-8 h. The reaction color
changed from colorless to dark blue. After this time, the reaction
mixture was quenched with water (2 mL), added all at once. The resulting
colorless mixture was then allowed to stir for 10 min. The organic layer
was decanted, and the solid residues were washed with an additional 3x10
mL Et2O. After separation, the combined organics were passed through a
Celite pad in a sintered glass funnel to afford a clear solution that was
concentrated on a rotary evaporator. The product 9,10-dihydroanthracene
was obtained as a white solid, yield 97%. 1HNMR (CDCl3) δ 7.29 (m, 2H),
7.19 (m, 2H), 3.93 (s, 2H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 136.5, 127.3, 126.0, 36.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reagent, Birch reduction, alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Birch reductions at room temperature with alkali metals in silica gel
(Na2K-SG(I))
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nandi, Partha; Dye, James L.; Jackson, James E.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(16), 5790-5792

