$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Ethyl 8-methoxy-1-methyl-1,4-dihydronaphthalene-1-carboxylate 15 Note: In
order to obtain a good yield of the desired alkylated Birch product
without contamination with products of simple Birch reduction it was
found to be crucial that the liquid ammonia dispensed from the cylinder
was first dried over sodium and then carefully distilled into the
reaction flask to remove water and traces of iron-containing impurities.
A 1 L three neck flask, fitted with a dry ice condenser and cooled to
-78°C in a dry ice-acetone bath, was charged with freshly distilled
liquid ammonia (500 mL). t-Butanol (4.8 mL, 50.16 mmol) was added,
followed by a solution of ethyl 8-methoxy-1-naphthoate (10.50 g, 45.60
mmol) in THF (100 mL). Lithium wire (3 mm; 0.79 g, 113.99 mmol) was added
piecemeal, the final piece of wire causing the pale yellow solution to
take on a permanent dark blue color. After addition was complete, the
dark blue solution was stirred for a further 5 min at -78°C and
iodomethane (8.5 mL, 136.80 mmol) was slowly added, causing the reaction
mixture to become bright yellow. The resulting solution was stirred at
-78°C for 30 min, and the yellow color faded to almost colorless over
this time. The cooling bath and condenser were removed and the reaction
mixture was stirred vigorously overnight at rt to allow the ammonia to
evaporate prior to work-up. Water (200 mL) and ether (200 mL) were added,
and the aqueous phase was extracted with ether (3 × 100 mL). The combined
ethereal extracts were washed with water (200 mL) and brine (200 mL),
dried (MgSO4) and concentrated. The title compound as a colorless oil
(10.90 g, 97%). Generally, further purification of this product was not
required, although filtration through a short pad of silica gel was
sometimes carried out to remove colored impurities. (Found [M + Na+],
269.1132. C15H18NaO3 + requires 269.1148); νmax (CHCl3)/cm-1 3012, 2983,
2938, 2839, 1727, 1583, 1427, 1583, 1482, 1439, 1260, 1240, 1135; δH (400
MHz; CDCl3) 7.19 (1H, t, J 7.9), 6.79 (1H, dd, J 7.9, 1.0), 6.73 (1H, br.
d, J 7.9), 5.95 (1H, dt, J 10.0, 3.6), 5.70 (1H, dt, J 10.0, 2.3),
4.21-4.17 (1H, m), 4.08-4.03 (1H, m), 3.78 (3H, s), 3.45 (2H, dd, J 3.0,
2.3), 1.53 (3H, s), 1.16 (3H, t, J 7.0); δC (100 MHz; CDCl3) 175.9 (C),
156.6 (C), 134.2 (C), 130.4 (CH), 127.23 (C), 127.19 (CH), 123.6 (CH),
121.0 (CH), 108.3 (CH), 60.6 (CH2), 55.1 (Me), 45.5 (C), 29.5 (CH2), 25.0
(Me), 14.2 (Me).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Birch reductive alkylation; dry liquid NH3 is crucial for alkylated Birch
product, key step, scalable
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Toward the Total Synthesis of Hygrocin B and Divergolide C: Construction
of the Naphthoquinone-Azepinone Core
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nawrat, Christopher C.; Kitson, Russell R. A.; Moody, Christopher J.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(7), 1896-1899

