$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for M-SG Birch Reductions.
In a 100 mL round-bottom flask equipped with a glass-coated magnetic stir
bar and a rubber septum, anthracene (178 mg, 1 mmol, 1 equiv) and
Na2K-SG(I) (420 mg, 40% w/w original loading of metal alloy in silica
gel; titrated reducing capacity 4.9 mmol electrons= 2.45 equiv40) were
placed under an inert atmosphere (in a He drybox). To this flask was
added 10 mL of anhydrous THF, and the mixture was stirred at room
temperature for 6-8 h. The reaction color changed from colorless to dark
blue. After this time, the reaction mixture was quenched with water (2
mL), added all at once. The resulting colorless mixture was then allowed
to stir for 10 min. The organic layer was decanted, and the solid
residues were washed with an additional 3x10 mL Et2O. After separation,
the combined organics were passed through a Celite pad in a sintered
glass funnel to afford a clear solution that was concentrated on a rotary
evaporator. The product 9,10-dihydroanthracene was obtained as a white
solid, yield 97%. Yield 96%. Information not present.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported reagent, Birch reduction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Birch reductions at room temperature with alkali metals in silica gel
(Na2K-SG(I))
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nandi, Partha; Dye, James L.; Jackson, James E.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(16), 5790-5792

