$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Representative procedure for the Birch
reductive alkylation of chiral benzamides with various iodides as
described for the synthesis of
(2'S,1S)-2-methyl-1-(4'-chlorobutyl)-1-[{(2'-methoxymethyl)pyrrolidinyl}carbonyl]-2,5-cyclohexadiene
9a Ammonia (360 mL) was stirred with FeCl3 (ca 100 mg) and Na (ca 1.2 g)
then was distillated into a 500 mL, three-necked, round-bottomed flask
equipped with a Teflon® stopper and a dry ice condenser at -78 °C under
nitrogen. A solution of amide 6 (1.7 g, 7.3 mmol) and tBuOH (0.70 mL, 7.3
mmol) in dry THF (25 mL) was added via syringe to the ammonia solution.
The mixture was vigorously stirred for 10 min then potassium (860.0 mg,
22.0 mmol) was added in small pieces until a dark green colour persisted
for 15-20 min. A solution of 4-chloro-1-iodobutane 8a (2.4 g, 11.0 mmol)
in dry THF (15 mL) was added at -78 °C and the resulting yellow mixture
was stirred for 1 h at -78 °C. The reaction mixture was quenched by the
addition of ammonium chloride (ca 4 g) in one portion at -78 °C and the
mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature. The ammonia was
evaporated under a stream of N2 overnight. To the residue was added
saturated aqueous ammonium chloride (200 mL) and the aqueous layer was
extracted with EtOAc (3 × 200 mL). The combined organic extracts were
washed with saturated aqueous sodium thiosulphate (200 mL), water (200
mL) and brine (200 mL) then dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated
at reduced pressure by rotary evaporation. The residual oil was purified
by flash chromatography (20 : 80 → 50 : 50 EtOAc-hexanes) to afford the
title compound (1.88 g, 79 %, 92% d.e.) as an orange oil that was stored
under nitrogen.
(2'S,1S)-2-Methyl-1-(3'-chloropropyl)-1-[{(2'-methoxymethyl)pyrrolidinyl}carbonyl]-2,5-cyclohexadiene
9b Birch reductive alkylation of benzamide 6 (619.7 mg, 2.7 mmol) with
commercially available 1-chloro-3-iodopropane (0.42 mL, 4.0 mmol) was
carried out as described for compound 9a. The title compound was obtained
as a colourless oil (614.0 mg, 74%) after purification by flash
chromatography (20 : 80 → 30 : 70 EtOAc-hexanes). NMR analysis
established that the title compound was isolated with a diastereomeric
excess of 92%. Major diastereomer: Rf 0.50 (40 : 60 EtOAc-hexanes); [α]D
20 -31.9 (c 1.0, CHCl3); IR (KBr plate neat) νmax 3010, 2960, 2870, 2815,
1625, 1450, 1390, 1380, 1190, 1110, 950, 700 cm-1; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
