$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Cis-1-tert-butyl 2,5-dimethyl 2H-pyrrole-1,2,5(5H)-tricarboxylate (11) A
solution of di-tert-butyl biphenyl (4.70 g, 17.7 mmol) in THF (250 mL)
was cooled to 0°C under an atmosphere of argon. Lithium wire (2.50 g, 353
mmol), which had been washed in pentane and scraped with a scalpel to
remove any oxide coating, was rapidly cut into small pieces (approx. 2 mm
length) and dropped into the THF solution under an atmosphere of argon.
After approximately 5 minutes a blue/green colour was observed. The LiDBB
solution was stirred at 0°C for 3 hours before being cooled to −78°C.
Pyrrole 3 (10.0 g, 35.3 mmol) in THF (150 mL) was added dropwise causing
the blue colour to be replaced by a brown colour. The reaction mixture
was stirred at −78°C for 16 hours. Di-tert-butyl phenol (29.1 g, 141
mmol) in THF (60 mL) was added dropwise and the reaction mixture was
stirred at −78°C for 30 mins. Saturated ammonium chloride solution (50
mL) was added and the reaction vessel removed from the ice-bath. After 20
minutes the reaction mixture was poured into H2O (100 mL), via a Buchner
funnel to remove any unreacted lithium wire, and the layers were
separated. The aqueous layer was extracted with ethyl acetate (3 × 200
mL). The combined organic layers were then dried over MgSO4, filtered and
the solvent was removed in vacuo. The crude product was purified by flash
column chromatography [SiO2, diethyl ether-light petroleum (bp 40-60°C),
4:6] to afford a pale yellow oil (8.8 g, 88%) as a >10:1 mixture of
diastereomers in favour of cis-dihydropyrrole 11. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
δH 5.93-5.85 (2H, m), 5.09-5.01 (2H, m), 3.75 (6H, s), 1.41 (9H, s); 13C
NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δC 169.61, 169.15, 153.0, 127.6, 127.4, 81.1, 66.9,
66.6, 52.5, 52.4, 52.0, 28.2, 28.0, 27.9. Spectroscopic data reported for
the cis pyrroline compound is identical to that reported in the
literature.2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An enzymatic approach to the desymmetrization of disubstituted pyrrolines
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Donohoe, Timothy J.; Rigby, Caroline L.; Thomas, Rhian E.; Nieuwenhuys,
William F.; Bhatti, Farrah L.; Cowley, Andrew R.; Bhalay, Gurdip; Linney,
Ian D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2006), 71(16), 6298-6301

