$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: D) General procedure for Birch reductive
alkylation: In a dry three-necked flask equipped with a dry-ice condenser
was introduced, under nitrogen, a biaryl (8 mmol) in THF (40 mL). In case
the starting material is a phenol, n-BuLi (2.5M sol. in hexane, 1.1 eq.)
was added dropwise at -78 °C and the solution was stirred for 10 minutes.
The flask was then cooled to -78 °C and ammonia (approx. 80 mL) was
condensed. Lithium wire (0.133 g, 19 mmol, 2.3 eq.) was added. The
solution was stirred either at -78 °C for 30 minutes in case of
"activated" biaryls (e.g. containing a 3,5-dimethoxyphenyl ring) or
stirred at -33 °C (refluxing NH3) for 1h for the others. The red mixture
was then cooled to -78 °C and chloroacetonitrile (1.6 mL, 24 mmol, 3 eq.)
in THF (10 mL) was added in one portion (Methyl chloroacetate was added
for 10a). The mixture turned immediately brown. After 5 minutes, ammonia
was let to evaporate and a half-saturated aqueous ammonium chloride
solution was added. Extraction with ether, washing with brine, drying
with sodium sulfate and evaporation of the solvents gave a brown paste,
which was purified by silica gel chromatography (Petroleum ether/EtOAc
mixtures)
[1-(4-Hydroxy-3-methoxy-phenyl)-3,5-dimethoxy-cyclohexa-2,5-dienyl]-acetonitrile
(16). This product was obtained as a viscous yellow oil (86%). - IR
(film, NaCl): ν = 3426 cm-1, 2938, 2250 (CN), 1694, 1515, 1263, 1206,
1146, 1022, 806, 736. - 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz): δ = 6.90-6.76 (m, 3H,
aromatic H), 5.73 (broad s, 1H, OH), 4.69 (s, 2H, 2 x vinylic H), 3.87
(s, 3H, OCH3), 3.60 (s, 6H, 2 x OCH3), 2.91 (AB system, Jab = 24.5 Hz,
2H, CHaHb), 2.89 (s, 2H, CH2CN). - 13C NMR (CDCl3, 62.9 MHz): δ = 153.1
(s, 2 x aromatic C), 146.5 (s, aromatic C), 144.5 (s, aromatic C), 138.5
(s, aromatic C), 118.3 (s, CN), 118,0 (d, aromatic CH), 114.2 (d,
aromatic CH), 109.2 (d, aromatic CH), 98.8 (d, 2 x vinylic CH), 56.0 (q,
OCH3), 54.6 (q, 2 x OCH3), 44.7 (s, aliphatic C), 32.5 (t, CH2CN), 31.1
(t, CHaHb). - HRMS [M]+• C17H19NO4: calcd 301.1314; found 301.1310.
