$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Birch Reduction; Typical Procedure: The aromatic compound (13.5 mmol) in
MeOH (5 mL) was added to NH3 (45 mL) condensed at -80°C. Small pieces of
sodium (78 mmol, 1.8 g) were then added. Once the sodium had disappeared
(after a few minutes), Et2O (100 mL) and water (100 mL) were added. NH3
was cautiously removed under vacuum. The aqueous layer was then extracted
with Et2O. The organic layers were dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and
concentrated under vacuum. The crude material generally contained more
than 95% of the desired product. Purifications were performed by rapid
silica gel chromatography under N2 using a mixture of pentane and Et2O in
the appropriate ratio as eluent. The final products were stored under
argon at -20°C. 4,7-Dihydrobenzo[1,3]dioxole (2a): This compound has a
low boiling point. For this reason, pentane had to be used for
extraction. Silica gel chromatography was performed using pentane/Et2O
8:2, yield 80%. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ = 2.9 (s, 4H, 2 x CH2C=), 5.6 (s, 2H, 2
x CH=), 5.7 (s, 2H, OCH2O). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ = 24.3, 97.5, 123.1, 131.0.
IR (neat): ν = 3035, 2870, 2836, 1764, 1352, 1218, 1174, 1069, 1035, 962,
912, 832 cm-1. MS (DCI/NH3): m/z = 125 (MH)+. Anal. Calcd for C7H8O2
(124.1): C, 67.77; H, 6.49; Found: C, 67.82; H, 6.60.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reinvestigation of Birch reduction of benzo[1,3]dioxoles and further
transformations of the resulting dihydro compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Sylvain, Catherine; Wagner, Alain; Mioskowski, Charles
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1998), (7), 970-972

