$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method A: (a) Ammonia (70 mL), was condensed
into a heat gun dried, three-necked round-bottomed flask equipped with
dry-ice condenser, mechanical stirrer and maintained at -78 °C, under a
slight positive pressure of dry nitrogen, (b) A solution of an α
-tetralone (1a-d, 16.4 mmol) in ether (8 mL) and tert-butanol (2 mL, 19
mmol), was introduced via a double needle and potassium (1.4 g; 36 mmol)
was then added in small portions. After the addition was complete, the
resulting blue suspension was stirred for 15 minutes, (c) To this
suspension, anhydrous lithium bromide (3.14 g; 36 mmol)was then added and
the mixture stirred vigorously for 30 minutes keeping the temperature at
-78 °C. Method B: The procedures for the reductive alkylations with MOMCl
or BOMCl were carried out using ether as co-solvent for the reduction
step, to facilitate its elimination as it is necessary to replace the
solvent during the alkylation step. The procedure for the Birch reduction
followed the same procedure steps (a), (b) and (c) as described in Method
A. At this point the cooling bath was removed, the ammonia was allowed to
evaporate, and the co-solvent was then removed in a stream of dry
nitrogen. Dry benzene or toluene was added and the mixture cooled at 0
°C, and the alkylating agent (32.1 mmol freshly destilled from CaCl2 )
was added. The mixture was allowed to stir for 15 minutes and then brine
(40 mL) and ether (30 mL) were added. The pH was adjusted to 7.5 by
addition of saturated NaHCO3 followed by the usual work-up: the aqueous
layer was then separated and extracted with more ether (4x25mL and EtOAc
(4x 25 mL). The combined ether extract was washed with brine, dried with
anhydrous Na2SO4, filtered and evaporated.
8a-Methoxymethyl-1,2,3,4,6,8a-hexahydro-naphthalen-1-one (2b)8b: Starting
from α -tetralone 1a, following the procedure described as method B.
(Ketone 1a, 1040 mg, 7.1 mmol; K, 694 mg, 17.8 mmol; tert-butanol 8 mL,
8.5 mmol; MOMCl, 16.2 mmol) produced compound 2b, 1.04 g (5.4 mmol, 78%)
as a yellowish oil and 0.266g of a 1:1 mixture of 2b and 2j Compound 2b8b
IR νmax (film): 2950, 2870, 1630, 1450, 1250, 1210, 1060, 980, 820 and
760 cm-1. 1H NMR δ: 1.6-2.5 (m, 6H, aliphatic protons), 2.64 (m, 2H, C-6
H), 3.30 (s, 3H, OCH3), 3,70 (d, 1H, J=9.0 Hz, CH20CH3), 3.50 (d, 1H, J=9
Hz, CH2OCH3), 5.7 (m, 2H, C-7 H), 6.02 (dt, 1H, J=10.0 and 2.0 Hz, C-8
H); 13C NMR (Cl3CD) ppm: 24.9 (C-3), 26.0 (C-6), 30.9 (C-2), 38.1 (C-4),
52.3 (C-8a), 59.0 (-OCH3), 76.7 (CH2OCH3), 120.2 (C-5), 122.8 (C-7),
128.6 (C-8), 129.7 (C-4a), 208 (C-1).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
