$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Table 4 Entries 1-2: Reductive alkylation of Methyl
5-Methoxy-3-(trimethylsilyloxymethyl) benzoate (4) with iodomethane. A
mixture of 620 mg (2 mmol) of ester 4 and 148 mg (2 mmol) of tert-butyl
alcohol was placed in a dry 100 mL 3-necked round bottom flask equipped
with a magnetic stir bar, a cold finger condenser topped with a nitrogen
line, a low temperature thermometer, and a septum. The system was placed
under a nitrogen atmosphere and dry tetrahydrofuran (10 mL) was added via
syringe. The septum was replaced with a gas inlet adapter attached to an
ammonia tank. The cold finger condenser was charged with dry iceacetone
and the reaction flask was also cooled in a dry ice-acetone bath. Ammonia
(approximately 30 mL) was condensed in the reaction vessel over a period
of about 10 min and then the gas inlet adapter was replaced with a glass
stopper. The stirred solution was cooled to an internal temperature of
-65 °C and 67 mg (9.5 mmol) of lithium metal was added in small pieces
(32 mg + 10 mg + 10 mg + 10 mg + 5 mg = 67 mg), through the stoppered
hole of the reaction flask, over a period of 40 min. The solution
maintained a deep blue color for 10 min after addition of the last piece
of lithium at which point 852 mg (6 mmol) of iodomethane was added via
syringe through the stoppered hole of the reaction flask. The blue color
dissipated after addition of the first 10 μL of halide after which the
remaining halide was added in one portion. The mixture was stirred for 30
min at -65 °C and 267 mg (5 mmol) of solid ammonium chloride was added
through the stoppered hole. The cold finger condenser was quickly removed
(after removing the nitrogen line), emptied, and returned to the reaction
flask (without the nitrogen line), and the cold bath was removed. The
stirred solution was allowed to warm to approximately -28 °C over a
period of 15 min. A water bath was placed under the reaction flask and
the reaction temperature increased to 15 °C over a period of 30 min. To
the residue was added 15 mL of water followed by 30 mL of benzene. The
phases were separated and the organic phase was dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated in vacuo (25-45 torr at a temperature below 40 °C) to give
621 mg of a colorless liquid. The residue was purified by chromatography
over 17 g of flash silica gel (loaded and eluted with hexanes-ethyl
acetate = 20:1) with collection of 10 mL fractions. Fractions 9-15 were
pooled and concentrated in vacuo to give 500 mg (76%) of 35 as a
colorless oil. This material was contaminated with small amounts of
compound 36 (7 mol %) based on 1H NMR spectroscopy. When the reaction was
performed using 296 mg (4 mmol) of tert-butyl alcohol the product (35)
(also contaminated with 36 as described above) was isolated in 61% yield.
500 mg (76%) of 35 as a colorless oil IR (neat) 1734 cm−1; 1H NMR (C6D6,
400 MHz) δ 0.0 (two s, 6H), 0.92 (s, 9H), 1.48 (s, 3H), 2.79 (br s, 2H),
3.22 (s, 3H), 3.33 (s, 3H), 3.92 (s, 2H), 4.81 (s, 1H), 5.90 (s, 1H); 13C
NMR (C6D6, 100 MHz) δ −5.3, 18.4, 26.0, 28.4, 29.4, 46.6, 51.5, 53.7,
66.5, 97.0, 124.0, 134.4, 154.1, 175.6; exact mass calcd for C17H30O4Si
(M + Na)+ m/z 349.1811, found m/z 349.1803.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternate reaction conditions gave a lower yield, incremental addition
(Li in stage 2)
