$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Birch Reductive
Alkylation. A solution of 1 (2a or 6)(1.82 g, 12.4 mmol) and tert-butyl
alcohol (1.16 mL, 1.0 equiv) in THF (50 mL) was cooled to -78 °C, and
ammonia (700 mL) was added. Lithium (0.38 g, 3 equiv) was added in small
pieces, and after 15 min, excess metal was consumed by the addition of
1,3-pentadiene (0.8 mL). Methyl iodide (0.38 mL, 4 equiv) in THF (3 mL)
was added, and the reaction mixture was stirred at -78 °C for 1 h.
Ammonia was allowed to evaporate, water was added, and the mixture was
extracted with methylene chloride (3 x 150 mL). The combined organic
layers were washed with 10% sodium thiosulfate, dried over MgSO4,
filtered, evaporated, and purified by flash chromatography on silica gel
(hexane/ethyl acetate 2:1) to afford pure samples.
7a-Ethyl-2-methyl-2,3,5,7a-tetrahydroisoindol-1-one (4b). Isolated as an
oil (74%). 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 0.82 (t, 3 H), 1.60 (m, 2 H), 2.65 (m, 2 H),
2.87 (s, 3 H), 3.73 (d, 1 H), 4.05 (d, 1 H), 5.82 (m, 1 H), 5.95 (m, 1
H), 5.99 (d, 1 H); CIMS m/z (rel intensity) 178 (M+ + 1, 100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Birch redn.-alkylation reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Organic synthesis methodology. Preparation and diastereoselective Birch
reduction-alkylation of 3-substituted 2-methyl-2,3-dihydroisoindol-1-ones
