$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Birch Reduction-Allylation. To a solution of
benzamide (1.0 eq.) and tert-butyl alcohol (1.0 eq.) in THF (10 mL/mmol
amide) and NH3 (130 mL/mmol amide) at -78 °C was added alkali metal in
small pieces until a blue coloration was maintained for 20 min.
Piperylene was added dropwise to consume the excess metal, and then allyl
bromide (2.5 eq.) was added. The solution was stirred at -78 °C and
allowed to slowly warm to room temperature to allow the NH3 to evaporate.
Water was added and the mixture was extracted with CH2Cl2. The organic
layer was washed with brine, dried (Na2SO4) and concentrated in vacuo to
give 2,5-cyclohexadiene product. Pure product for analysis was obtained
by column chromatography (3:7 EtOAc/hexanes).
((R)-1-Allyl-2-methoxy-5-methylcyclohexa-2,5-dienyl)((S)-2-(methoxymethyl)pyrrolidin-1-yl)methanone
(4). Use of the general procedure with 3a and potassium provided a 72%
yield. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 5.70-5.52 (m, 1 H), 5.09 (d, 1H, J=1.4 Hz),
4.98-4.89 (m, 2 H), 4.72 (t, 1H, J=3.6 Hz), 4.35-4.25 (m, 1 H), 3.62 (dd,
1 H, J=9.5, 3.2 Hz), 3.61-3.49 (m, 1H), 3.49 (s, 3 H), 3.34(s, 3 H),
3.31-3.24 (m, 2 H), 2.81-2.72 (m, 2 H), 2.66-2.45 (m, 2 H), 1.95-1.70 (m,
7 H). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δu 135.2, 121.3, 92.7, 58.9, 58.1, 54.2, 22.2; δd
170.5, 153.1, 133.5, 116.4, 72.0, 52.7, 46.1, 41.2, 31.6, 26.4, 24.8. IR
(film) 1618 cm-1. GC tR=17.75 min.(major 99.11%), 17.84 (minor 0.89%).
d.r. 111:1. EI-MS m/z (%): 305 (M+, 5), 264 (9), 163 (55), 162 (66), 149
(78), 142 (100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
