$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM In an oven dried three-necked round bottom flask equipped with a water
condenser was introduced, under nitrogen, the biarylic precursor (3 g,
11.5 mmol) in THF (60 mL). n-BuLi (5.06 mL, 2.5M soln. in hexane, 1.1
eq.) was then added dropwise at -78°C and the solution was stirred for 30
min. The flask was then cooled to -78°C and ammonia (120 mL) was
condensed. Lithium wire (0.2 g, 28.7 mmol, 2.5 eq.) was added. The
solution was then stirred at -78°C for 30 min. The red mixture was then
cooled to -78°C and chloroacetonitrile (2.2 mL, 34.5 mmol, 3 eq.) in THF
(15 mL) was added in one portion. The mixture turned immediately brown.
After 10 min., ammonia was let to evaporate and a half-saturated aqueous
ammonium chloride solution was added (150 mL). After extraction with
AcOEt (3 x 100 mL), the reaction media was washed with brine, dried over
sodium sulfate and the organic solvents were concentrated under vacuum to
provide a brown paste. The crude product was then submitted to silica gel
flash chromatography (Petroleum ether/AcOEt : 80/20) which led to the
product ethanesulfonic acid
[2-(1-cyanomethyl-cyclohexa-2,5-dienyl)-phenyl]-carbamic amide, yield 2.4
g, 70%. yellow solid, m.p = 124.5-125.1 °C. IR (solid, KBr): ν = 2953,
1718, 1522, 1431, 1346, 1196, 975, 756, 661 cm-1.1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz):
δ (ppm) = 7.60-7.49 (m, 1H), 7.35-7.25 (m, 1H), 7.18-7.12 (m, 3H),
6.31-6.18 (m, 2H), 5.70-5.58 (m, 2H), 3.13 (q, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 3.01-2.95
(m, 2H), 2.93 (s, 2H), 1.31 (t, J = 7.1 Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 75.5
MHz): δ (ppm) = 137.2 (Cq), 130.1 (Cq), 129.3 (CH), 128.8 (CH), 128.3
(CH), 125.3(CH), 124.2 (2CH), 119.8 (2CH), 117.0 (Cq), 46.9 (CH2), 41.2
(Cq), 30.6 (CH2), 26.0 (CH2), 8.1 (CH3). MS (ESI) m/z (%): 325 [M+Na]+
(100).HRMS (ESI): [M+Na]+ C16H18N2O2NaS: calcd 325.0987; found 325.0977
(8.5 ppm). Element. Anal. Calcd for C16H18N2O2S (302.1): C 63.55, H 6.00,
N 9.26, S 10.60; found: C 63.56, H 6.03, N 9.12, S 10.24.
