$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Birch
Reduction-Allylation. To a solution of benzamide (1.0 eq.) and tert-butyl
alcohol (1.0 eq.) in THF (10 mL/mmol amide) and NH3 (130 mL/mmol amide)
at -78 °C was added alkali metal in small pieces until a blue coloration
was maintained for 20 min. Piperylene was added dropwise to consume the
excess metal, and then allyl bromide (2.5 eq.) was added. The solution
was stirred at -78 °C and allowed to slowly warm to room temperature to
allow the NH3 to evaporate. Water was added and the mixture was extracted
with CH2Cl2. The organic layer was washed with brine, dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated in vacuo to give 2,5-cyclohexadiene product. Pure product
for analysis was obtained by column chromatography (3:7 EtOAc/hexanes).
((R)-1-Allyl-5-(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl)-2-methoxycyclohexa-2,5-dienyl)((S)-2-(methoxymethyl)pyrrolidin-1-yl)methanone
(8). Use of the general procedure with 7 and lithium afforded a 70%
yield. 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 6.99-6.95 (m, 2H), 6.85 (d, 1 H, J=8.2 Hz), 5.75
(s, 1 H), 5.72-5.61 (m, 1 H), 5.03-4.86 (m, 3 H), 4.35-4.25 (m, 1 H),
3.91 (s, 3 H), 3.89 (s, 3 H), 3.66-3.50 (m, 2 H), 3.55 (s, 3 H), 3.36 (s,
3 H), 3.36-3.30 (m, 2 H), 3.30-3.10 (m, 2 H), 2.86 (dd, 1 H, J=14, 7 Hz),
2.68 (dd, 1 H, J=14, 7 Hz), 1.95-1.61 (m, 4 H). 13C NMR (CDCl3) δu 135.1,
122.1, 117.5, 111.1, 108.5, 92.7, 58.9, 58.2, 56.0, 54.4; δd 170.1,
152.7, 148.9, 134.9, 132.7, 117.0, 72.0, 53.0, 46.1, 41.5, 28.9, 26.4,
25.0. IR 1617 cm-1. NP-HPLC tR=28.500 min (major), 31.338 (minor);
d.r.=>99:1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
