$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Birch Reductive Alkylation. A solution of 1 (2a
or 6)(1.82 g, 12.4 mmol) and tert-butyl alcohol (1.16 mL, 1.0 equiv) in
THF (50 mL) was cooled to -78 °C, and ammonia (700 mL) was added. Lithium
(0.38 g, 3 equiv) was added in small pieces, and after 15 min, excess
metal was consumed by the addition of 1,3-pentadiene (0.8 mL). Methyl
iodide (0.38 mL, 4 equiv) in THF (3 mL) was added, and the reaction
mixture was stirred at -78 °C for 1 h. Ammonia was allowed to evaporate,
water was added, and the mixture was extracted with methylene chloride (3
x 150 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with 10% sodium
thiosulfate, dried over MgSO4, filtered, evaporated, and purified by
flash chromatography on silica gel (hexane/ethyl acetate 2:1) to afford
pure samples. 2,7a-Dimethyl-2,3,5,7a-tetrahydroisoindol-1-one (4a).
Isolated as a light yellow oil in 69% isolated yield (1.26 g). 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ 1.12 (s, 3 H), 2.62 (q, 2 H), 2.81 (s, 3 H), 3.69 (d, J = 12.2
Hz, 1 H), 4.02 (d, J = 12.5 Hz, 1 H), 5.67 (br, 1 H), 5.78 (m, 1 H), 6.04
(dd, J = 9.3, 1.2 Hz, 1 H); IR (film) 2900, 1650, 1415, 1385 cm-1; CIMS
m/z (rel intensity) 164 (M+ + 1, 100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Birch redn.-alkylation reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Organic synthesis methodology. Preparation and diastereoselective Birch
reduction-alkylation of 3-substituted 2-methyl-2,3-dihydroisoindol-1-ones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Guo, Zihong; Schultz, Arthur G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2001), 66(6), 2154-2157

