$DATUM 110-54-3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM D) General procedure for Birch reductive alkylation: In a dry
three-necked flask equipped with a dry-ice condenser was introduced,
under nitrogen, a biaryl (8 mmol) in THF (40 mL). In case the starting
material is a phenol, n-BuLi (2.5M sol. in hexane, 1.1 eq.) was added
dropwise at -78 °C and the solution was stirred for 10 minutes. The flask
was then cooled to -78 °C and ammonia (approx. 80 mL) was condensed.
Lithium wire (0.133 g, 19 mmol, 2.3 eq.) was added. The solution was
stirred either at -78 °C for 30 minutes in case of "activated" biaryls
(e.g. containing a 3,5-dimethoxyphenyl ring) or stirred at -33 °C
(refluxing NH3) for 1h for the others. The red mixture was then cooled to
-78 °C and chloroacetonitrile (1.6 mL, 24 mmol, 3 eq.) in THF (10 mL) was
added in one portion (Methyl chloroacetate was added for 10a). The
mixture turned immediately brown. After 5 minutes, ammonia was let to
evaporate and a half-saturated aqueous ammonium chloride solution was
added. Extraction with ether, washing with brine, drying with sodium
sulfate and evaporation of the solvents gave a brown paste, which was
purified by silica gel chromatography (Petroleum ether/EtOAc mixtures)
[1-(3-Hydroxy-phenyl)-cyclohexa-2,5-dienyl]-acetonitrile (6). This
product was obtained as a white solid (68 %) and could be recrystallized
in DCM/hexane. - m.p. 106.4-108.6 °C. - IR (solid, KBr): ν = 3343 cm-1,
2269 (CN), 1612, 1586, 1483, 1330, 1274, 1230, 840, 789, 738, 700. - 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 250 MHz): δ (ppm) = 7.21 (t, J = 8.2 Hz, 1H, aromatic H),
6.86-6.69 (m, 3H aromatic H), 6.05-5.98 (m, 2H, vinylic H), 5.76-5.67 (m,
2H, vinylic H), 5.50 (broad s, OH), 2.88-2.65 (m, 2H, CHaHb), 2.82 (s,
2H, CH2CN). - 13C NMR (CDCl3, 62.9 MHz): δ (ppm) = 156.1 (s, aromatic C),
146.4 (s, aromatic H), 130.0 (d, aromatic CH), 129.4 (d, 2 x vinylic CH),
126.3 (d, 2 x vinylic CH), 118.2 (d, aromatic CH), 117.9 (s, CN), 114.2
(d, aromatic CH), 113.7 (d, aromatic CH), 42.3 (s, aliphatic C), 30.1 (t,
CH2CN), 26.1 (t, CHaHb). - MS (SIMS) m/z (%): 234 [M+Na]+ (100), 212
[M+H]+ (50). - HRMS [M+Na]+ C14H13NONa: Calcd 234.0895; found: 234.0896.
- Anal. Calcd for C14H13NO (211.26): C 79.59, H 6.20, N 6.63; found: C
79.26, H 6.26, N 6.45.
