$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Method A: (a) Ammonia (70 mL), was condensed
into a heat gun dried, three-necked round-bottomed flask equipped with
dry-ice condenser, mechanical stirrer and maintained at -78 °C, under a
slight positive pressure of dry nitrogen, (b) A solution of an α
-tetralone (1a-d, 16.4 mmol) in ether (8 mL) and tert-butanol (2 mL, 19
mmol), was introduced via a double needle and potassium (1.4 g; 36 mmol)
was then added in small portions. After the addition was complete, the
resulting blue suspension was stirred for 15 minutes, (c) To this
suspension, anhydrous lithium bromide (3.14 g; 36 mmol)was then added and
the mixture stirred vigorously for 30 minutes keeping the temperature at
-78 °C. (d) Finally, an alkylating agent (methyl iodide, allyl bromide:
32 mmol) was added, and the mixture was stirred for 15 minutes. The
cooling bath was removed, and the ammonia was allowed to evaporate. The
residue was diluted with brine (40 mL) and ether (40 mL), the pH of the
solution was adjusted to 7.5 by careful addition of cold 10 % HCl, the
aqueous layer was then separated and extracted with more ether (4x25mL
and EtOAc (4x 25 mL). The combined ether extract was washed with brine,
dried (anhydrous Na2SO4), filtered and evaporated.
1,8a-Dimethyl-1,2,3,4,6,8a-hexahydro-naphthalen-1-one (2d): Starting from
8-methyl, 1-tetralone 1b, following the procedure described as method A,
(1b, 1.60g 10 mmol; ether 5.5 mL; K 0.85g, 21.6 mmol; tert-butanol 1.22
mL, 11.6 mmol; MeI 19.5 mmol). A (4:6) mixture of starting ketone 1b and
compound 2d were obtained. Flash chromatography did not allow for the
complete separation of the products, therefore the mixture was submitted
directly to the L-selectride® reduction to prepare 3g (see experimental
for 3g). (1H NMR δ: 5.80-5.91 (m, 2H), 5.69 (brs, 1H), 5.56 (brs, 1H),
2.68-2.30 (m, 6H), 2.10-1.90 (br m, 2H), 1.76 (brs, 3H), 1.29 (s, 3H,
C-8a CH3) ppm.)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Studies of Birch reductive alkylation of substituted α-tetralones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Labadie, Guillermo R.; Cravero, Raquel M.; Gonzalez-Sierra, Manuel
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2000), 30(22), 4065-4079

