$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Birch reduction of anthracene and its
derivatives-General procedure. A sodium amalgam (1%, 0.1 g Na, 10.0 g Hg)
was prepared and N,N-dimethylformamide added, followed by nickel(II)
complex 2 (2.5 equiv.). The resultant suspension was stirred under argon
for 4.5 h during which time the suspension turned from colourless to dark
red. The dark red solution was added to the substrate (1.0 equiv.)
rapidly via cannula and stirred under argon at room temperature for 1 h.
After this time, the reaction mixture was added to a saturated solution
of ammonium chloride (150 ml) to quench and the aqueous solution
extracted with diethyl ether (2 × 150 ml). The combined organic layers
were washed with water (2 × 100 ml) and brine (100ml), then dried with
sodium sulfate and concentrated in vacuo. Purification by silica gel
chromatography afforded the corresponding dihydro derivative. Compound
12c-Ethyl 9,10-dihydroanthracene-10-carboxylate. Light yellow crystalline
solid (30 mg, 59%). (Found: (ESI) [M+NH4]+, 270.1841. C17H16O2 requires
[M+NH4]+, 270.1489); νmax (KBr disc/cm-1) 3067, 3024, 2981, 2935, 2873,
1732, 1482, 1454, 1293, 1216, 1185, 1150, 1027; δH (500 MHz, CDCl3) 1.17
(3H, t, J 7.1, CH3), 3.92 (1H, d, J 18.1, HCH), 4.06 (2H, q, J 7.1, CH2),
4.36 (1H, d, J 18.1, HCH), 5.00 (1H, s, CHCO2Et), 7.25-7.28 (4H, m, ArH),
7.35-7.37 (2H, m, ArH), 7.41-7.43 (2H, m, ArH); δC (126 MHz, CDCl3) 14.0
(CH3), 35.7 (CH2) 53.1 (CH), 61.1 (CH2O), 126.4 (CH), 127.4 (CH), 127.9
(CH), 128.1 (CH), 133.9 (C), 136.7 (C), 171.9 (C); m/z (CI) 270
([M+NH4]+, 100%), 253 (24), 179 (32).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Birch reduction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reductions of Challenging Organic Substrates by a Nickel Complex of a
Noninnocent Crown Carbene Ligand
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
